    "title": "Black or African American students in Greene County lagged behind average college readiness rate in 2023-24 school year",
    "text": "In the 2023-24 school year, 54.9% of Black or African American students in Greene County schools met Alabama’s college readiness criteria, according to the Alabama Department of Education .\nOf the 74 students assessed for college readiness in the county, 39 were Black or African American and met college readiness standards—unchanged from the previous year.\nA total of 61 students graduated from Greene County school in the 2023-24 school year.\nAlabama’s educational system was rated as one of the worst in the U.S. , according to a 2023 study from Scholaroo. The state was ranked 46th based on factors such as school quality, student success, and teacher-to-student ratio.\nEthnicities’ College Readiness and Graduation Rates Throughout Greene County in 2023-24 School Year Ethnicity Graduation Rate College Ready Black or African American 83.1% 54.9%",
